# CMake builds in place, next to the project it built.
build/
# A sweep configures one tree per variant, named for the variant it built.
build-*/
# Packed apps land here; they are outputs, not sources.
*.uapp
# The linker writes this map beside the ELF it describes.
*.elf.elf.map
SleepLab/**/build/
# Cargo builds in place as well, and a target/ tree is nobody's source.
target/

# TouchGFX's code generator keeps its own scratch beside the sources it emits;
# only the emitted sources are worth committing.
generated/**/cache/
generated/**/UnicodeList*.txt

# Claude Code. The shared commands and the project instructions are tracked;
# worktrees and scratch files under .claude/ are local to one machine.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
